    "forensics": "The losing cluster is driven by mid-day liquidity droughts (10:35\u201314:10 IST) where low-follow-through breakouts either reverse rapidly into stop losses (e.g., TATASTEEL 5-minute whipsaw and consecutive re-entry on Oct 22) or stagnate into EOD square-offs. Furthermore, the \u20b951.29 fee drag severely erodes expectancy, turning flat or marginally positive gross trades (like TATASTEEL Trade #6 with \u20b93.36 gross profit) into net losses.",
    "learning": "In Indian NSE cash equities, high-volume sweeps (2.85x) occurring after the initial morning institutional discovery phase often represent exhaustion absorption rather than trend initiation; expanding target thresholds while tightening stop-loss bounds and breakeven triggers is essential to overcome statutory brokerage/STT friction on small \u20b910,000 capital allocations.",
